                <head>No. 166<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>The Committee of Ministers of the Council of Europe met in Strasbourg May 6–7,
                    but no discussion of the draft treaty of the European Political Community took
                    place. According to telegram 330 from Strasbourg, May 8, which briefly
                    summarized the meetings, the draft treaty was barely mentioned, and the general
                    feeling among all the Ministers was that the Foreign Ministers of the six
                    countries concerned should first come to a decision before the draft treaty was
                    discussed by the Committee of Ministers. (740.00/5–853)</p>
                <p>No significant action concerning the draft treaty occurred during the first part
                    of the Fifth Ordinary Session of the Consultative Assembly of the Council of
                    Europe, which met in Strasbourg May 7–13. For a record of these meetings, see
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Minutes of Proceedings</hi> (Strasbourg, 1953) and
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Official Report of Debates</hi> (Strasbourg,
                    1953).</p>
            </div>
